===Interjection===
{{en-interj}}

# {{lb|en|slang}} [[nonsense|Nonsense]]!
#* '''1843''', [[w:Charles Dickens|Charles Dickens]], ''[[w:A Christmas Carol|A Christmas Carol in Prose, Being a Ghost Story of Christmas]]'', [[s:A Christmas Carol (Dickens, unsourced ed.)/Stave 1|stave 1]],
#*: ‘A Merry Christmas, uncle! God save you!’ cried a cheerful voice. It was the voice of Scrooge’s nephew, who came upon him so quickly that this was the first intimation he had of his approach.
#*: ‘Bah!’ said Scrooge, ‘'''Humbug'''!’

===Verb===
{{en-verb|humbugs|humbugging|humbugged}}

# {{lb|en|slang}} To play a [[trick]] on someone, to [[cheat]], to [[swindle]], to [[deceive]].
# {{lb|en|slang|obsolete}} To waste time talking.
# {{lb|en|US|African American Vernacular|slang}} To [[fight]], to act tough.

